      "summary": ": Rāpare/Thursday The crisp, clear and fabulously sunny days just keep rolling in and they make for some lovely days on the maunga. The snowmaking team are on a run worthy of a Commonwealth Games medal, fattening up the trails and developing terrain. The groomers have had another great night - the cord will ski/ride beautifully this morning. Off trail still offers plenty of fun chalkiness in places, and with the summit and chutes open, there's plenty to offer advanced explorers. \"Give others room\" is a key message in the NZ Snow Code, and patrol will be out enforcing reponsible and respectful skiing/riding on Triple Treat. Please be considerate of others so we all have a great day. Start your day fueled up with one of the legendary breakfast burritos from the cafe, and hit the slopes. Big Skite opens mid morning after race training. -- Closed as of checking: Matukituki Basin, Sundance",
